    "英文": "Iidabashi Station (飯田橋駅, Iidabashi-eki) is a major interchange railway station which straddles Tokyo's Chiyoda, Shinjuku and Bunkyō wards. It was originally built as Iidamachi Station (albeit in a slightly different location), terminus of the then Kōbu Railway, precursor to today's Chūō Line. The Ōedo Line addition to the station in 2000 was designed by architect Makoto Sei Watanabe.\n\n",
    "中文": "飯田橋站（日語：飯田橋駅／いいだばしえき，羅馬化：Iidabashi eki）是位於日本東京都千代田區、新宿區、文京區，屬於東日本旅客鐵道（JR東日本）、東京地下鐵、東京都交通局（都營地下鐵）的鐵路車站。各站的所在地參見車站資訊模板內的記述。"
